      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "VINKE B NZ (3) stayed out of the early speed battle from a wide gate on the front line last start and couldn't come on, finishing 23 metres from the winner in eighth at Menangle over 1609m. Likely to get all the favours from this better draw. Ideally placed and is sure to be there at the finish. MAJOR CRUNCH (7) continued a strong run of recent form and deserved his win last start, scoring by a neck over 2040m at Redcliffe. Will need a bit of luck negotiating a very wide starting position. His last-start form is good enough to put him right in the finish. UNCLE TONY (6) didn't do a bad job when fourth over 1660m at this track last time out. BARRACUDA NZ (5) is in the mix following a fourth at his most recent appearance over 1660m at this track. Racing in an easier line-up today rates well as one of the leading chances.",
